Libussa_10_2_455                Libussa_10_2_455                He hath taken me. He hath taken the best of me, and left nothing but a shell. In his home of bone, in his halls of skin, behind his walls of flesh, he hath taken all I had.
Libussa_10_2_456                Libussa_10_2_456                I walked, and under my feet the floor did quiver. I looked, and beheld that I trod upon the bloated belly of one even more wretched than I.
Libussa_10_2_457                Libussa_10_2_457                Once I had the faith of an innocent. He did ravage me, and took my faith away, into his cathedral of flesh, where the soft and dripping walls swallow all sound. Even the sound of my screams. It fed him. And he grows. Like gel-sacs of rot on decaying wood, he grows.
Libussa_10_2_458                Libussa_10_2_458                He will awaken soon. My innocent faith fed him, and made him stronger. Soon he will be strong enough to awaken, and defile the purity of the world, as he defiled me. My soul is beyond all salvation, and soon all souls will be damned as well.
Garinol_11_1_2520               Garinol_11_1_2520               Now make haste to thy University, and bestow my gratitude upon noble Ecaterina. I shall meet with her anon, and plan the defense of Prague against the fiends.
Wilhem_11_1_491                 Wilhem_11_1_491                 Now that the golem is dead, we must visit Josef, leader of clan Nosferatu. The Jewish quarter of Prague falls under his control, and our custom dictates that we tell him of the events. Be warned: the Nosferatu embrace curses them with transfiguration of face and body. They chose to live out of sight of the mortals and their fellow Cainites. But they have wisdom beyond even that of the Brujah.
Josef_12_1_492                  Josef_12_1_492                  But not wisdom enough to prevent this night's slaughter.
Wilhem_12_1_493                 Wilhem_12_1_493                 Salutations from Ecaterina the Wise.
Josef_12_1_494                  Josef_12_1_494                  Wise? Not wise enough to protect the mortals from Cainite treachery. And neither was I.
Wilhem_12_1_495                 Wilhem_12_1_495                 It has now been set right, by the courage of the Promethian Brujah!
Josef_12_1_496                  Josef_12_1_496                  Has it? Another quarter of Prague is now defenseless before the fiends who steal innocents in the night. Sons of Caine and sons of Abel alike are missing. But I am pleased thou hast stopped the golem. Send my greetings to thy Mistress.
Christof_12_1_497               Christof_12_1_497               Where do these many passages lead?
Wilhem_12_1_498                 Wilhem_12_1_498                 Everywhere. Everywhere mortals live in Prague. There are secret entrances to even the most impregnable fortresses of the mortals.
Christof_12_1_499               Christof_12_1_499               Most useful.
Josef_12_1_500                  Josef_12_1_500                  Enter them not, stripling! Trespass, and I will peel thy pretty, unscarred face and wear it as a fair and tender mask. My tunnels are only for Nosferatu.
Wilhem_12_1_501                 Wilhem_12_1_501                 Or those who pay the price.
Christof_12_1_502               Christof_12_1_502               What price?
Josef_12_1_503                  Josef_12_1_503                  Bring me a goblet of sweet blood from an elder Cainite of beautiful visage. Or venture not within my lair.
Christof_11_1_462               Christof_11_1_462               Can the Rabbi control this brute?
Prague2_11_1_1800               Prague2_11_1_1800               Save us! Our own Golem has gone mad!
Mendel_11_1_463                 Mendel_11_1_463                 Yes. But the Rabbi is dead. I am his son, Mendel.
Christof_11_1_464               Christof_11_1_464               Tell me how to kill the Golem, Mendel?
Mendel_11_1_465                 Mendel_11_1_465                 The Golem's life cometh from Truth.
Christof_11_1_466               Christof_11_1_466               Thou speakest riddles.
Mendel_11_1_467                 Mendel_11_1_467                 The word "Truth" hath been writ upon a scroll and placed within the brow of the creature. The Hebrew word for "Truth" and the word for "Death" are but a single letter apart. Destroy that one letter, and the creature falls in death.
Christof_11_1_469               Christof_11_1_469               The demon is no more.
Mendel_11_1_470                 Mendel_11_1_470                 The Golem was no demon.
Christof_11_1_471               Christof_11_1_471               It was, and we have sent it straight to hell.
Mendel_11_1_472                 Mendel_11_1_472                 The Golem was animated by the life force, and his spirit now returns to Abraham's bosom.
Christof_11_1_473               Christof_11_1_473               What? Blaspheming Sorcerer! This monster of clay has no soul!
Mendel_11_1_474                 Mendel_11_1_474                 I am no Sorcerer. I am a Kabbalist. And all life is from God. Every man, animal, and creature. Even this Golem. Even Vampires such as thee.
Christof_11_1_475               Christof_11_1_475               Liar! Thou dost toy with my sanity! One such as I cannot be redeemed. I am an outcast from heaven!
Mendel_11_1_476                 Mendel_11_1_476                 Not so. All life comes from one place, and to that place it must return.
Christof_11_1_479               Christof_11_1_479               Why should God make such creatures?
Mendel_11_1_480                 Mendel_11_1_480                 To vex mankind. They are all part of the Kingdom of God, sent to test our faith, as the Devil did test the simple faith of Job. How hast thy faith endured, Crusader?
Christof_11_1_481               Christof_11_1_481               Not well. For God hath abandoned my soul.
Mendel_11_1_482                 Mendel_11_1_482                 The question is not whether God hath abandoned thee, selfish boy. It's whether thou wilt abandon God. And become a beast.
Christof_11_1_487               Christof_11_1_487               I shall consider thy words.
Mendel_11_1_488                 Mendel_11_1_488                 Nay, there is no magic in the Shem. 'Tis merely letters.  Letters which connect the golem to the true Source of power.
Wilhem_11_1_489                 Wilhem_11_1_489                 Nonetheless, the Cappadocians would be grateful to get such a thing. It would help them build golems for their own protection.
Mendel_11_1_490                 Mendel_11_1_490                 The Shem is thine, with my blessings, to do with as thou pleaseth.
Wilhem_13_1_505                 Wilhem_13_1_505                 Hail, Garinol of Clan Cappadocian, Master of the art of death.
Garinol_13_1_506                Garinol_13_1_506                Hail to thee, servant of the wise Ecaterina of Clan Brujah. Be most welcome. And hail to thee, good Christof, who vanquished the fiend in the mines. I make no claim of vengeance against thee for the destruction of my Haven. Instead, I offer my thanks to thee, and to thy clan for bringing to light the treachery of my venomous Childe Mercurio.
Christof_13_1_507               Christof_13_1_507               I present this to thee, as a gift from Ecaterina the Wise, Sire of the Brujah.
Garinol_13_1_508                Garinol_13_1_508                Ah, yes! This should be of some use, some use indeed, to protect us from the disorder of these times. Tell your mistress I am grateful, and owe the noble Brujah a boon.
Christof_13_1_509               Christof_13_1_509               We shall.
Garinol_13_1_510                Garinol_13_1_510                I only wish this shem had not been purchased at so dear a price. I mourn the blood shed in the Jewish quarter by the wicked Mercurio, and do reproach myself for his misdeeds. The good Rabbi now journeys into the land of the dead where hides all knowledge, and I am to blame.
Garinol_13_1_511                Garinol_13_1_511                Prithee tell Ecaterina that I wish to serve her Promethian task, and strive with her to bind up our uncertain future. In partial payment of the boon I owe, I offer thee my prized Childe, Serena. She will aid thee in thy efforts.
Serena_13_1_512                 Serena_13_1_512                 I pray that my service will be of value to thee.
Christof_11_1_468               Christof_11_1_468               This is the Kabbalistic magic that quickened the golem!
Christof_13_1_504               Christof_13_1_504               Garinol pursues the lore of the golem, and may have use for this shem. I wish to deliver it to him, that he may learn to use lifeless clay in the stead of his hapless victims.
Wilhem_9_1_452                  Wilhem_9_1_452                  The Golem has run amok in the Jewish Quarter. Come quickly. Innocent lives are at stake.
Wilhem_11_1_451                 Wilhem_11_1_451                 We are too late!
Christof_11_1_459               Christof_11_1_459               The streets run crimson with innocent blood. This devastation strikes at my heart.
Wilhem_11_1_460                 Wilhem_11_1_460                 The golem was to be the protector of the Jews. But it hath become the agent of their destruction.
Wilhem_11_1_461                 Wilhem_11_1_461                 Mercurios' perfidy hath yielded great suffering.
Unorna_10_1_453                 Unorna_10_1_453                 A comely young sister did come to me from the convent. A clever lass she was, and more valorous than many a young warrior. She bade me give thee this letter.
Christof_14_2_530               Christof_14_2_530               This place is as great as the palace of any mortal Prince.
Brandl_14_2_531                 Brandl_14_2_531                 We know of these disappearances. Little happens in Prague without our knowledge.
Ecat_14_2_532                   Ecat_14_2_532                   How now? Hast thou discovered the culprit?
Brandl_14_2_533                 Brandl_14_2_533                 We can direct thee aright. Should we feel so moved.
Ecat_14_2_545                   Ecat_14_2_545                   I cannot imagine such a thing as can move thy lordship.
Brandl_14_2_534                 Brandl_14_2_534                 We desire a reliquary containing the arm of Saint George, which lieth in the antechamber of the cathedral of St. Vitus. Alas, a ring of hallowed ground outside the cathedral doth repel Cainites. The sanctified ground extends not into the cathedral, but we cannot cross the outer gates.
Cosmas_14_2_535                 Cosmas_14_2_535                 Then how may WE cross the sanctified ring to enter the cathedral?
Brandl_14_2_536                 Brandl_14_2_536                 We tire of thee. Pray do not return until thou hast the arm.
Ecat_14_2_537                   Ecat_14_2_537                   Very well. We go.
Christof_14_2_539               Christof_14_2_539               Nay! To withhold such knowledge is wicked! We seek to save many! Has the Prince no pity, no humanity, that he only bestows his knowledge for a price?
Christof_14_2_538               Christof_14_2_538               If we must.
Brandl_14_2_540                 Brandl_14_2_540                 I warn thee, stripling! We have staked fledglings for a hundred years as punishment for little else than speaking in our presence. We allowed thy mistress to make thee, and we can unmake thee with a word.
Cosmas_14_2_541                 Cosmas_14_2_541                 Pray forgive him. Christof knows not-
Brandl_14_2_542                 Brandl_14_2_542                 Silence! Because yon Childe Christof did show bravery in the silver mines, and may yet be useful to us, he shall yet retain his freedom. But only if he henceforth silences his impertinent Brujah tongue.
Christof_14_2_2500              Christof_14_2_2500              ... (say nothing)
Ecat_14_1_514                   Ecat_14_1_514                   I am not surprised the little nun is missing. She is reckless.
Christof_14_1_515               Christof_14_1_515               Dost thou know of her?
Cosmas_14_1_516                 Cosmas_14_1_516                 No!
Ecat_14_1_517                   Ecat_14_1_517                   Yes. We shall lie to thee no longer. Anezka came hither in search of thee. The gift of sight blazed in her eyes, revealing unto her that we are Childer of Caine. And yet she had no fear of us.
Christof_14_1_518               Christof_14_1_518               Where is she?
Cosmas_14_1_519                 Cosmas_14_1_519                 We told her thou wert not among us, and she left.
Christof_14_1_520               Christof_14_1_520               What?!
Ecat_14_1_521                   Ecat_14_1_521                   She insisted on leaving this letter for thee. As if she somehow knew we had lied to her. I give it thee.
Christof_14_1_523               Christof_14_1_523               Why didst thou not tell me?
Cosmas_14_1_524                 Cosmas_14_1_524                 Whelp! Thou must leave her world behind!
Christof_14_1_525               Christof_14_1_525               Thou hast doomed her! I could have persuaded her to stay in the safety of the convent
Ecat_14_1_526                   Ecat_14_1_526                   Nay. Thou canst not control such as she. There was a mania that shone in her eye- a kind of madness- and yet her mind was sharp. As if her delirium had strengthened her mind rather than sapped it. In another time I would have been moved to take such a one as my Childe.
Christof_14_1_527               Christof_14_1_527               Nay! Her soul must remain pure! We must find her and save her from the fiends! We must redeem her before my curse dooms her, as in my dream!
Cosmas_14_1_528                 Cosmas_14_1_528                 The nun was not the only one missing. Many have been taken- mortal and vampire alike. We go in search of our Brujah allies, but will rescue as many of the others as we can. Including thy mortal nun.
Ecat_14_1_529                   Ecat_14_1_529                   Therefore we are resolved to entreat Prince Rudolf Brandl for assistance. Even though he is of clan Ventrue! To make amends for withholding this letter from thee, we go tonight. Come!
Christof_14_1_513               Christof_14_1_513               Noooo!
Wilhem_15_1_568                 Wilhem_15_1_568                 Behold, Christof. There are worse fates than death. And worse than unlife as a vampire.
Christof_15_1_569               Christof_15_1_569               Thou spoke true.
Wilhem_15_1_556                 Wilhem_15_1_556                 These are Caitiff, the clanless vampires. Many have been rejected by their Sires, but some descend from many generations of Caitiff.. With no wisdom to stave off the Beast, they have lost all humanity, and become monsters. Look well upon them, for they are our future. Our compassion is all that stands between us and them.
Christof_15_1_557               Christof_15_1_557               Then truly we are damned.
Serena_15_1_558                 Serena_15_1_558                 Damned? Christof, thou art the pinnacle of creation! Thou hast powers surpassing even the most virtuous man. Thou art a law unto thyself, more god than man! Thou art immortal! An angel in form and power! RELISH thy station! SAVOR the exquisite power thy God hast visited upon thee! Use it to wreak thy will upon a world of sinners.
Ilig_15_1_559                   Ilig_15_1_559                   The path of Caine is the only escape, follow it, let it lead you...
Christof_14_3_549               Christof_14_3_549               We crave a goblet of thy precious blood, that we may enter the Nosferatu tunnels to pass into the Cathedral.
Ecat_14_3_550                   Ecat_14_3_550                   I do give thee a goblet of my blood, brave Christof. May the arm of a saint arm us with absent friends.
Christof_14_3_551               Christof_14_3_551               I seek to enter thy tunnels, and in return I offer thee the blood of the most beautiful Ecaterina.
Christof_14_3_546               Christof_14_3_546               Josef, do thy hidden tunnels allow vampires to enter the Cathedral?
Josef_14_3_547                  Josef_14_3_547                  Aye. My tunnels undermine the sanctified ring of protection. I have used the tunnels to enter the Cathedral many times, and gorged myself upon the intoxicating Christian blood within.
Christof_14_3_548               Christof_14_3_548               Then I shall bring thee the blood of a beautiful Cainite elder, and enter thy tunnels.
Josef_14_3_552                  Josef_14_3_552                  Oh yes! It is lovely. Most lovely. Thou mayst enter my halls. Go thou. However I cannot guarantee a safe journey.
Brandl_15_1_2522                Brandl_15_1_2522                Fiends and warlocks cavort upon our very doorstep, and neonates presume upon our Princely patience?  Be gone!
Christof_16_1_570               Christof_16_1_570               Behold the reliquary with the arm of Saint George. I pray thee tell us of those that are missing.
Brandl_16_1_571                 Brandl_16_1_571                 Yes. Thou hast done well. We shall tell thee a tale to curdle thy blood. Thy absent friends and vanished allies now dwell in Vienna, at the Chantry of the damnable clan Tremere. They abduct mortals and turn them into ghouls, that they may have footsoldiers in their bloody war against the Tzimisce. But now the Tremere have undertaken to abduct their fellow vampires, in violation of all Cainite law! They conjoin the flesh of many vampires to create demonic gargoyles to fight the Tzimisce. Such are the ways of those that did once plunder the power of Caine by committing an unspeakable act upon a grandchilde of Caine.
Ecat_16_1_572                   Ecat_16_1_572                   Where have they taken the slaves?
Brandl_16_1_573                 Brandl_16_1_573                 We know not. But our spies have ferreted out their slave master. His name is Ardan, and he dwelleth in a secret Tremere chantry hidden within an alchemist shop in Golden Lane.
Ecat_16_1_574                   Ecat_16_1_574                   We seek thy Princely permission to attack him and liberate such slaves as he has taken.
Brandl_16_1_575                 Brandl_16_1_575                 Such dispensation I do not give lightly, for we of clan Ventrue have lately joined in an alliance with the Tremere. We do use the Tremere for our own ends against the hated Tzimisce clan. Yet for their crimes against my city, the Tremere must pay a debt of blood. We do bestow our princely dispensation upon thee. Thou mayst assault Ardan's chantry, and liberate such Cainite slaves as he has taken.
Christof_16_1_2521              Christof_16_1_2521              May we liberate mortal slaves as well, or does the Prince care not for those whose blood sustains us?
Christof_16_1_2501              Christof_16_1_2501              ... (say nothing)
Brandl_16_1_577                 Brandl_16_1_577                 I see that Ecaterina the Wise has not yet tamed the impertinent tongue of this Childe. I shall assist her in the chore.
Brandl_16_1_578                 Brandl_16_1_578                 Now that thou hast paid the price, I give thee full dispensation to liberate such mortals as thou findeth within Ardan's chantry. Now get thee from my sight.
Ecat_16_1_579                   Ecat_16_1_579                   I thank my lord.
Brandl_16_1_580                 Brandl_16_1_580                 Now go.
Serena_14_4_553                 Serena_14_4_553                 I understand thy sorrow, Christof. When Garinol Embraced me I was forced to leave behind all I loved in the mortal world. The loss of it still weighs upon my heart, and drags me to despair. I offer thee any comfort I may give in thy grief.
Christof_14_4_554               Christof_14_4_554               I thank thee, but I do not surrender my hope of reunion with Anezka, even though I am beyond all hope.
Serena_14_4_555                 Serena_14_4_555                 Then thy Anezka is fortunate indeed, though such barren hope might breed only more sorrow.
Vaclav_15_1_565                 Vaclav_15_1_565                 Who is it disturbeth the repose of the dead?
Christof_15_1_566               Christof_15_1_566               One who prizes the living over the dead.
Vaclav_15_1_567                 Vaclav_15_1_567                 Thou hast entered the halls of King Vaclav I! Thy Cainite flesh must be unraveled from thy Cainite bones, that thou may enter the Halls of the Dead naked of all but thy Cainite spirit.
Ardan_17_6_602                  Ardan_17_6_602                  Do not attack me! I shall give thee all thy desires.
Erik_17_6_603                   Erik_17_6_603                   I desire only thy death, snake of a wizard!
Christof_17_6_604               Christof_17_6_604               Hold! Ardan, I am Christof Romuald of Clan Brujah. Where is Anezka?
Ardan_17_6_605                  Ardan_17_6_605                  Welcome, Christof Romuald. Ah, yes. An intriguing woman came unto me. A nun, she was, and she was my first nun. That is, she was the first nun who ever came seeking me. Anezka, her name. She sought the lore of the Kindred. She sought our secrets. And she sought to learn of  thee, Christof. I was intrigued with such audacity.
Christof_17_6_606               Christof_17_6_606               Come to the point, Magus.
Ardan_17_6_607                  Ardan_17_6_607                  She seemed to have no fear. No fear at all. I was dumbstruck. She seemed possessed of the courage of a hundred warriors. Yet I could smell her fear. Well aware she was of the risk she ran. Was she filled with arrogant self-righteousness? No. She knew her God would not protect her from my hunger. Did she seek martyrdom? No. She clearly clung to her life, and lived life with a passion I had not seen before in a nun. Was she mad? Or a mere fool? No. Behind her quiet words there lurked a cunning mind. She was.. she was... I did not know what she was. And in not knowing, I was intrigued. Intrigued, and... strangely... drawn to her.
Christof_17_6_608               Christof_17_6_608               I care not for thy loathsome appetites, Ardan. What became of her?
Ardan_17_6_609                  Ardan_17_6_609                  And she was quite beautiful. Didst thou know? Couldst thou see that behind her wimple, that her hair was long and auburn? Couldst thou see that beneath the shapeless folds of her robe that she possessed a body as achingly beautiful as any odalisque? Truly she chose the wrong profession to make the best use of the gifts God had bestowed upon her. In defiance of Heaven, she had buried her talents in the field of the Holy Orders. Her beauty transfixed me, just as her courage thrilled me. I had never met a woman like her, and I shall never again. I had to have her. I had to make her my own Childe.
Christof_17_6_610               Christof_17_6_610               If thou dared to defile her in such a way, I swear I will burn thee to ash an inch at a time.
Ardan_17_6_611                  Ardan_17_6_611                  Thou might show more charity toward the only one who can find her.
Erik_17_6_612                   Erik_17_6_612                   He baits thee, Christof, and dawdles for some treacherous purpose! Pray let me kill him!
Christof_17_6_613               Christof_17_6_613               Ardan, If thou dost fail to tell me where she is with thy next breath, Erik will behead thee  before thou draw breath again.
Ardan_17_6_614                  Ardan_17_6_614                  I know not! I touched her not, but merely sent her away to the Tzimisce.
Christof_17_6_615               Christof_17_6_615               Dost thou take me for a fool? Why wouldst thou send one thou lusted for to thy hated enemy?
Ardan_17_6_616                  Ardan_17_6_616                  My Sire would not allow me another Childe and I dared not defy him! But I could not bear the thought of another Embracing her. So I sent her to the Tzimisce. They are the only clan that would have no use for one such as she, so I could be sure they would not Embrace her. They would simply kill her, thinking her a part of some Tremere scheme.
Christof_17_6_617               Christof_17_6_617               Devil-tongued fiend! Thou hast sent her to her death! Die!
Ardan_17_6_618                  Ardan_17_6_618                  Wait! She did return from the Tzimisce!
Christof_17_6_619               Christof_17_6_619               What?
Serena_17_6_620                 Serena_17_6_620                 Liar! The Tzimisce would have killed her!
Christof_17_6_621               Christof_17_6_621               Peace! Let him speak!
Ardan_17_6_622                  Ardan_17_6_622                  I asked her how she survived, and she said her faith sustains her in all things. She even thanked me for sending her to the Tzimisce. Ah! A most remarkable woman! My spies did tell of a Premysl Revenant that did cower before the pure light of her faith, and, sobbing like a child, whispered to her of... Golconda!
Christof_17_6_623               Christof_17_6_623               Golconda? What is that?
Ardan_17_6_624                  Ardan_17_6_624                  The belief that a vampire can be redeemed! Cured of the blood of Caine! 'Tis but a legend, and no more, told to give comfort to weak-willed Cainites. Yet no one knows more of Golconda than the great Tremere master Etrius. She said she would go to him in his Chantry in Vienna. She even asked to ride to Vienna in our October caravan of slaves. What a woman!
Christof_17_6_625               Christof_17_6_625               Where is she?! Tell me or I split thee in twain!
Ardan_17_6_626                  Ardan_17_6_626                  I delivered her to the Ventrue caravan driver, Orsi, and they left three days ago for Vienna.
Christof_17_6_627               Christof_17_6_627               Dog! Thou hast enslaved her!
Ardan_17_6_628                  Ardan_17_6_628                  Hah! Master Etrius will take great delight in her! And now I have finished casting the spell that will destroy thee, thou love-struck clotpole!
Erik_17_6_629                   Erik_17_6_629                   Arrr! Ardan, I will slay thee if it is my last act on earth!
Wilhem_17_6_2524                Wilhem_17_6_2524                Ecaterina will rejoice in our victory! Come! We return to the University in triumph!
Christof_17_6_630               Christof_17_6_630               Very well. But then I shall go to Vienna, and reclaim fair Anezka from these cursed warlocks!
Christof_18_1_631               Christof_18_1_631               I must take my leave of this city, I am sure the Tremere hold Anezka in their Vienna chantry. I can no longer continue here while she remains in danger.
Ecat_18_1_632                   Ecat_18_1_632                   Ardan was a consummate deceiver. The Tremere have gathered fearsome power in Vienna, and we are not ready for bloody battle with the Usurpers! They invited thee to play a sinister game. They know that one day we will have to attack their Vienna Chantry, and so they desire to force our hand before we are ready. I shall not be tricked. Only after we have gathered the other clans in alliance may we contemplate a strike against them. We will not venture into so palpable a trap.
Christof_18_1_633               Christof_18_1_633               I understand.
Christof_18_1_634               Christof_18_1_634               But Anezka will die.
Ecat_18_1_635                   Ecat_18_1_635                   Many have died in the Elder wars. And many more will die 'ere Gehenna comes. But fewer will die if we bide our time, and heed not the trickery of the Tremere.
Christof_18_1_636               Christof_18_1_636               That is wise.
Christof_18_1_637               Christof_18_1_637               But I cannot simply abandon Anezka to those fiends.
Ecat_18_1_638                   Ecat_18_1_638                   Thou canst and thou must! Thy claim upon her is born in weak-kneed mortal sentiment. Release such frailties, and spare thyself further wretchedness. We cut our ties to mortals when first we receive the blessing of Allfather Caine. Thou hast been reborn in blood, cleansed of mortal claims! Thou art exalted! Thou art immortal! Thou art finally free!
Christof_18_1_639               Christof_18_1_639               Yes! I reject her. Nothing ties me to the life I once had.
Christof_18_1_640               Christof_18_1_640               I thought we Promethians respect the mortals.
Christof_18_1_641               Christof_18_1_641               I see.
Ecat_18_1_642                   Ecat_18_1_642                   For a bumpkin of a holy warrior, thou dost reason like a Greek sage. Aye, we respect mortal men. But we do not seek kinship with the current breed. For lo these many generations, mortals have been cowed by the cleverness of the Inconnu, their faculties oer'thrown by scheming Mages, and their wisdom tainted by demons. The little nobility left in them is tainted by corrupt rulers and priests. The mortals of Carthage were worthy companions. Their base progeny are not worth the spilling of the blood of immortals.
Christof_18_1_643               Christof_18_1_643               Aye. Anezka is a mere mortal. I will not spill my blood for her.
Christof_18_1_644               Christof_18_1_644               Anezka is as noble a woman as any in Carthage. We must rescue her.
Christof_18_1_645               Christof_18_1_645               I understand.
Ecat_18_1_646                   Ecat_18_1_646                   Very well. Let us hear no more of the matter.
Christof_18_1_648               Christof_18_1_648               I understand thy wisdom. But still I wish her rescued.
Christof_18_1_647               Christof_18_1_647               I obey. I will no longer seek to save her.
Ecat_18_1_649                   Ecat_18_1_649                   Brazen brat! Thou hast earned no such right! Even faithful Wilhem would quake in fear before making such a selfish request.
Christof_18_1_651               Christof_18_1_651               Perhaps. But I make it all the same.
Christof_18_1_650               Christof_18_1_650               Very well. I withdraw it. I will not seek to rescue her.
Ecat_18_1_652                   Ecat_18_1_652                   Mayhap in a generation or two shalt thou be deemed worthy of making such a request.
Christof_18_1_654               Christof_18_1_654               In a generation or two she will die an old woman even if she survives the Tzimisce.
Christof_18_1_653               Christof_18_1_653               Forgive me. I pay thou one day find me worthy of such requests.
Ecat_18_1_655                   Ecat_18_1_655                   Then let her die! She chose her path, not thee. She chose to enter the world of Vampires. Thou canst not save the foolhardy from their own reckless ways. Remember, like Caine, we are not our brother's keepers.
Christof_18_1_656               Christof_18_1_656               I dragged her down in this vile pit, and I will draw her back again.
Christof_18_1_657               Christof_18_1_657               True. She did not have to leave the convent. I cannot save her.
Ecat_18_1_658                   Ecat_18_1_658                   I forbid it! Tread lightly, lest thou arouse my anger and provoke my powers upon thee!
Christof_18_1_659               Christof_18_1_659               Do as thou must unto me, but I must rescue her. I know not the fate of my soul,  only the state of my heart.
Christof_18_1_660               Christof_18_1_660               Very well. I submit to thy rule.
Ecat_18_1_663                   Ecat_18_1_663                   Thou hast chosen aright.
Ecat_18_1_665                   Ecat_18_1_665                   Very well. I see thy heart is fixed upon this course, and thou will not be denied. Go if thou wilt. Shouldst thou survive the Tremere trap, remember well this freedom I have bestowed upon thee. But I shall not attend this fool's errand. Only a Malkavian would follow thee.
Ecat_18_1_661                   Ecat_18_1_661                   Thou hast chosen aright.
Wilhem_18_1_666                 Wilhem_18_1_666                 Then call me a moon-mad Childe of Malkav, for I shall go.
Wilhem_18_1_662                 Wilhem_18_1_662                 I do re-christen thee Peter, for, like the apostle, thou hast denied her that thou lovest.
Wilhem_18_1_664                 Wilhem_18_1_664                 So be it, Judas. Thou hast betrayed her that thou lovest.
Christof_18_1_668               Christof_18_1_668               I forbid it. This is my errand.
Christof_18_1_667               Christof_18_1_667               Wilhem! Thou art true a friend as any in God's kingdom!
Wilhem_18_1_669                 Wilhem_18_1_669                 Then I shall tie thee like a hog and carry thee to the Tremere lair in Vienna. . I too shall not be denied.
Christof_18_1_670               Christof_18_1_670               Thou art a true friend.
Wilhem_18_1_671                 Wilhem_18_1_671                 A true fool. Mayhap I shall yet see this God of whom thou art overmuch fond.
Christof_18_1_672               Christof_18_1_672               Or mayhap we shall tear the foul halls of the Tremere down around their scabrous ears, and bring the black heart of their sire to Ecaterina to wear as a charm.
Ecat_18_1_673                   Ecat_18_1_673                   Wilhem, thou art mad! Two Cainites cannot survive Die Haus de Hexe!
Erik_18_1_674                   Erik_18_1_674                   Not two. Three shall go. Though I have no wish to see the inside of another Tremere Chantry, I shall discharge my life boon by accompanying the brave Brujah who pried open the jaws of the Tremere trap and released poor Erik.
Serena_18_1_675                 Serena_18_1_675                 Where Christof goes, Serena goes. Mayhap four shall prevail where one cannot.
Ecat_18_1_676                   Ecat_18_1_676                   Mayhap I shall have to replace four Promethians!
Christof_18_1_677               Christof_18_1_677               Come, we leave for Vienna.
Christof_17_1_581               Christof_17_1_581               This shop is but a mask, concealing the face of the Tremere in their lair.
Christof_17_5_2523              Christof_17_5_2523              Hold! What manner of Cainite have they imprisoned here? He seems more animal than man...
Erik_17_5_598                   Erik_17_5_598                   Thou hast saved Erik of Clan Gangrel. According to the ancient Cainite law, I owe thee a life boon. I shall accompany thee and protect thee until such time as I discharge my debt.
Christof_17_5_599               Christof_17_5_599               Thou speaks with honor.
Erik_17_5_600                   Erik_17_5_600                   Thy providential attack did interrupt the wicked sorcerer Ardan as he began a conjuration to twist me into a mindless gargoyle. At the sound of thy coming, the Tremere snake slithered into the chambers below! I am thine to command – after I have felt the Tremere's shriveled heart burst between my jaws!
Christof_17_5_601               Christof_17_5_601               Thou mayst tear the warlock's heart from his chest only after I have pried truthful answers from his mouth. Now let us go.
Serena_17_2_586                 Serena_17_2_586                 We have found the roots of the great trees, and perhaps the root of Tremere power.
Wilhem_17_2_587                 Wilhem_17_2_587                 What wickedness do they brew here?
Ecat_18_1_678                   Ecat_18_1_678                   Then the matter is settled.
Wilhem_18_1_679                 Wilhem_18_1_679                 Come, we leave for Vienna.
Christof_18_1_680               Christof_18_1_680               What?
Serena_18_1_681                 Serena_18_1_681                 Ecaterina hath learned that important Brujah were imprisoned on Orsi's caravan to Vienna. We must make all haste to overtake them.
Wilhem_18_1_682                 Wilhem_18_1_682                 Strange, is it not, that thou art given leave to travel after Anezka only after thou hast forsaken her.
Wilhem_19_1_683                 Wilhem_19_1_683                 This means traveling through the Bohemian forest, it is beset with Werewolves, mortal enemies of our kind. Few Cainites survive the road.
Erik_19_1_684                   Erik_19_1_684                   There will be no trouble with the Moon-beasts while I am near. My clan has made peace with these creatures, we will have safe passage through the forest.
Christof_19_1_685               Christof_19_1_685               Very well. Let us leave by the east gate.
Christof_17_4_593               Christof_17_4_593               We have found prisoners!
Wilhem_17_4_594                 Wilhem_17_4_594                 Thou art free of thy bondage by the power of the Promethians.
Prague2_17_4_595                Prague2_17_4_595                Thanks upon thanks to thee for releasing us!
Prague2_17_4_596                Prague2_17_4_596                Ye have saved us surely! Blessings upon ye, stranger.
DATrem2_17_2_588                DATrem2_17_2_588                How dare any enter the chantry of the House Tremere uninvited?
DATrem2_17_2_589                DATrem2_17_2_589                Thou shalt pay dearly for thy crimes!
DATrem2_17_3_590                DATrem2_17_3_590                Tut tut. We must mollify thy distemper with slow dismemberment.
DATrem2_17_3_591                DATrem2_17_3_591                Perhaps thou wilt be more compliant when thy body parts are pickled in great vats for later use in our experiments
DATrem2_17_3_592                DATrem2_17_3_592                I wish to see thy blood bubble up from thy body, burning with mage fire.
Christof_17_1_582               Christof_17_1_582               What wonders are these? 'Tis as if the Tree of Knowledge and the Tree of Life have rooted in this terrible place.
Serena_17_1_583                 Serena_17_1_583                 These are magicked trees. The Tremere revel in their Thaumaturgical power to reshape the world to their purposes.
Christof_17_1_584               Christof_17_1_584               Even the humble fruits of the earth are weapons to the Tremere.
Serena_17_1_585                 Serena_17_1_585                 Then let us reap a harvest of unliving mages.
DABart2_20_3_706                DABart2_20_3_706                Speak up, stranger. Dost thou crave wine, ale, or spirits?
Friedrich_20_2_699              Friedrich_20_2_699              Be thou welcome in the weapon shop of Friedrich Von Zweter. There are no finer weapons in all Vienna than are herein.
Christof_20_2_700               Christof_20_2_700               We seek mended armor.
Friedrich_20_2_701              Friedrich_20_2_701              Thou hast an impoverished look , and the demeanor of outlanders. Hast thou the coin to pay?
Erik_20_2_702                   Erik_20_2_702                   If such uncharitable suspicion is the custom of the land, I am glad to be an outlander.
Christof_20_2_703               Christof_20_2_703               We are merely weary and dusty from the road. We can pay our way.
Serena_20_2_704                 Serena_20_2_704                 We can pay in gold or in blood. The choice is thine, Von Zweter.
Friedrich_20_2_705              Friedrich_20_2_705              Er... Yes. How may I be of service?
Christof_20_4_713               Christof_20_4_713               They are magically sealed, we must find a way to enter through the barrier.
Christof_20_1_698               Christof_20_1_698               The Haus de Hexe...
Christof_22_5_812               Christof_22_5_812               Another Tremere!
Erik_22_5_813                   Erik_22_5_813                   Nay! He is mortal. I can smell it!
Wilhem_22_5_814                 Wilhem_22_5_814                 Aye. Not Tremere, but a mortal mage of the order that splintered into the Tremere. He may be useful.
Christof_22_5_815               Christof_22_5_815               Hail to thee, mage. I am Christof, of Clan Brujah.
Orvus_22_5_816                  Orvus_22_5_816                  Hail to thee, I am Orvus, mage of the Hermetic Order.
Christof_20_3_708               Christof_20_3_708               We are looking for a Ventrue named Orsi. Canst thou tell us where we may find him?
Christof_20_3_707               Christof_20_3_707               They're Cainites, perhaps they know where to find this Orsi.
Kazi_20_3_709                   Kazi_20_3_709                   Come to his mansion, in the western Ringstrasse, tonight there is a feast in honor of the new solstice. Here is an invitation, on the finest virgin skin parchment.
Christof_20_3_710               Christof_20_3_710               I like not this talk of the skin of virgins.
Kazi_20_3_711                   Kazi_20_3_711                   Hee hee hee...
Christof_20_5_714               Christof_20_5_714               This must be the house of Count Orsi, the slave master.
Erik_20_5_715                   Erik_20_5_715                   All the fops, bootlicks and and toadies in Vienna are here assembled.
Kazi_20_5_2526                  Kazi_20_5_2526                  So! Christof has not yet perished at the hands of the vampire-priest! Hee hee...The deadly nature of thy mission inflames my sister Teta. And my sister Zil entreats me tell thee that she too is filled with lust for thee. She cannot resist the charms of an immortal so close to death's door.
Orsi_20_5_716                   Orsi_20_5_716                   Ah, Welcome, Cainites. I see thou hast met my Childer. This is Kazi, Teta, and Zil, the most beautiful daughters of Caine thou shalt ever meet. Unfortunately, Teta and Zil lost the ability to speak during their mortal lives, I found them in servitude to a rather harsh master that saw to it to remove their tongues. He was dealt with in a fitting fashion, eh, say my darlings?
Orsi_20_5_717                   Orsi_20_5_717                   Don't worry. Kazi is happy to speak for the three of them now.
Christof_20_5_718               Christof_20_5_718               We come seeking Brujah taken as slaves from Prague, a mortal woman among them.
Orsi_20_5_719                   Orsi_20_5_719                   Slaves? Oh yes! The slave business hath been so very delicious. Duke Leopold needed a force to beat back the Tzimisce, and the lo! The Tremere appeared as if by divine providence. The Tremere and Tzimisce battle each other with surpassing fury, and I humble Ventrue that I am, I profit from the selling of slaves to both clans. The Duke and I shall ensure that the Tremere win the war, but only after I have collected much treasure from the carnage. Then shall we destroy the wounded Tremere, as punishment for the blasphemy they committed upon the Antediluvian Salout.
Christof_20_5_720               Christof_20_5_720               Tell us of the October shipment from Prague.
Orsi_20_5_721                   Orsi_20_5_721                   Dost thou think me a fool, that I will give away that which thou wilt purchase? Presumptuous bumpkin! Shouldst thou wish to know of thy allies, thou shalt perform a mission for me.
Christof_20_5_722               Christof_20_5_722               Or we shall slice thy head halfway off thy neck. Then shalt thou beg to tell of our allies.
Christof_20_5_724               Christof_20_5_724               Very well.
Orsi_20_5_723                   Orsi_20_5_723                   The Duke himself protecteth my haven! Attack me, and thou shalt suffer the most grievous retribution! AND thou shalt never find thy wayward slaves. Now, enough of such talk. It is business that we have to discuss, no more. Come, come to my study where we may discuss this further. Mayhap thou shalt find some delicious morsels to refresh thee.
Orsi_20_5_725                   Orsi_20_5_725                   Excellent! I see we two are akin, Zealot. Come, come to my study where we may discuss this further. Mayhap thou shalt find some delicious morsels to refresh thee.
Orsi_20_5_726                   Orsi_20_5_726                   Pray sup with me. I trust that thou will find these hors d'oeuvres to thy liking. If they are not pleasing to the taste, we shall have them flogged!
Christof_20_5_727               Christof_20_5_727               State thy business, Orsi!
Orsi_20_5_728                   Orsi_20_5_728                   Well. I can see thou hast no courtly manners in thee, bumpkin. Listen well. The Tremere have clapped their slaves away in the Tremere Chantry Die Haus De Hexe- the most protected Haven in Vienna. So do not think to try to kill me to gain them. They are quite beyond my power. Only Duke Leopold could convince the Tremere to give up their slaves. The Duke is responsible for allowing the Tremere to lodge in Vienna, so the Tremere do his bidding. Assist my ally, the Duke, and he will owe thee a boon.
Christof_20_5_729               Christof_20_5_729               What does the Duke wish?
Orsi_20_5_730                   Orsi_20_5_730                   The end to the reign of the pestilential vampire-priest Luther Black. Years ago Luther was but a mortal priest of Stephansdom Church. A wayward Lasombra sought to rule Vienna by controlling the Church, and dared to Embrace Luther. We sent the sire to hell, but Luther locked himself away from the outside world. He hath retained a pitiable hold on the faith he had in life and sleeps by day upon a cross of pure silver. Quite uncomfortable, I assume, but he fancies himself a martyr. The Duke has been unable to remove this blasphemous member of the shadow-clan, since Luther is ensconced within a ring of holy ground.
Christof_20_5_731               Christof_20_5_731               Then how do we find him?
Orsi_20_5_732                   Orsi_20_5_732                   Better to ask how to BIND him! Thou cannot destroy him. The priest has strange powers beyond thy ken. But thou can restrain him.
Orsi_20_5_733                   Orsi_20_5_733                   Here are chains even Luther Black cannot break. I am a master of metal work, and I have forged these shackles from a new, unbreakable alloy. Thou mayst find them useful, and more reliable than the magics in thy blood. Destroy Luther Black, and the Duke will retrieve thy slaves.Orsi approaches one of the hanging victims, delicately slices open his neck and fills a fluted glass with his blood. Quickly licking the wound, it closes up leaving the victim stunned. The party is stunned to notice that the victim is the drunken man they had seen at the bar earlier. He gurgles softly and goes limp.
Orsi_20_5_735                   Orsi_20_5_735                   Not to my liking, I'm afraid. I prefer blood of a nobler sort. 'Tis my only vice...
Erik_20_5_736                   Erik_20_5_736                   Enough of this dainty preening and strutting! How do we reach the Lasombra?
Orsi_20_5_737                   Orsi_20_5_737                   Refinement is wasted on lumbering brutes such as thee. There will come a time when boorish churls are put in their place! (pause) Thou shalt find a concealed entrance to the church. Behind our famous astrological clock in the Inner Stradt is a hidden passage. Enter by night and wait inside for daylight, and thou may steal into the inner haven undetected.
Christof_20_5_738               Christof_20_5_738               We shall undertake thy mission.
Orsi_20_5_739                   Orsi_20_5_739                   Good. Now get thee hence.
Orsi_20_5_2529                  Orsi_20_5_2529                  Away with thee, return with news of the Lasombra's death.
Christof_21_1_777               Christof_21_1_777               Did we look upon the face of Golconda?
Wilhem_21_1_778                 Wilhem_21_1_778                 We have seen nothing but the face of a lunatic Lasombra in his death throes.
Serena_21_1_779                 Serena_21_1_779                 If such is Golconda, kindly tell the angels I prefer damnation.
Orsi_22_1_780                   Orsi_22_1_780                   Thou hast serviced me well. I am in thy debt. Alas, I did not become the greatest merchant in Vienna by paying my debts. Such expenses unbalance my tidy ledger books. Besides, I should like to deliver the news of the Lasombra's death to the Duke myself. Take them away.
Christof_21_1_744               Christof_21_1_744               Beware! The shadows live!
Erik_21_1_745                   Erik_21_1_745                   Then the shadows can die!
Luther_21_1_776                 Luther_21_1_776                 Salvation at last!
Luther_21_1_2528                Luther_21_1_2528                Why dost thou return? Draw yon switch to open the skylight, that God's glorious sun may wash over me one final time, and cleanse me of all my Cainite sins! Make haste! The sun could set and rise and set again 'ere thou finished so simple a task!
Christof_21_1_746               Christof_21_1_746               Why would Luther Black glorify the expulsion of Caine from the Garden?
Serena_21_1_747                 Serena_21_1_747                 Perhaps it reminds him of his own exile from humanity.
Luther_21_1_748                 Luther_21_1_748                 Whom seek thee?
Christof_21_1_749               Christof_21_1_749               The Lasombra Luther Black.
Luther_21_1_750                 Luther_21_1_750                 I am he. So. Thou hast come to kill me.
Christof_21_1_751               Christof_21_1_751               Aye.
Luther_21_1_752                 Luther_21_1_752                 Come then. Kill me if thou can. I await the sacrament of thy blade. And the chains of Orsi the betrayer.
Serena_21_1_753                 Serena_21_1_753                 Then wait no longer.
Erik_21_1_754                   Erik_21_1_754                   Aye. 'Tis rude to keep a Churchman waiting.
Christof_21_1_755               Christof_21_1_755               Hold. I do not seek thy death, Luther. I only wish the return of those innocents taken by the Tremere.
Luther_21_1_756                 Luther_21_1_756                 I care not for thy wishes, whelp! Attempt thy deed or begone!
Christof_21_1_757               Christof_21_1_757               Thou hast done nothing deserving of death.
Erik_21_1_758                   Erik_21_1_758                   Christof, do not play with thy food. 'Tis unseemly.
Christof_21_1_759               Christof_21_1_759               Why dost thou seek death so ardently?
Luther_21_1_760                 Luther_21_1_760                 The cup which my father hath given me. Shall I not drink it?
Christof_21_1_761               Christof_21_1_761               Blasphemer! The Lord hath not commanded thy death! Thou merely seek release from the bitterness of thy unlife.
Serena_21_1_762                 Serena_21_1_762                 For God's sake, Christof! Kill him! He wants to die!
Luther_21_1_763                 Luther_21_1_763                 I see that thou are like unto me, Christof. Thou too seek holy refuge from bitter unlife.
Christof_21_1_764               Christof_21_1_764               Once I sought that selfish goal. Now I wish only to save she whom I have imperiled.
Luther_21_1_765                 Luther_21_1_765                 Then thou art truly the one for whom I have prayed. If thou would redeem, redeem me!
Christof_21_1_766               Christof_21_1_766               I shall not kill thee.
Luther_21_1_767                 Luther_21_1_767                 Please! I beg of thee! I cannot enter heaven if I turn my hand against myself. But thou! Thou has it in thy power to deliver me! T'would be an act of holiness.
Christof_21_1_768               Christof_21_1_768               If I take up thy burden, thou wouldst remain blameless, and thy sin would be mine alone to bear. Thy elevation would be my damnation.
Luther_21_1_769                 Luther_21_1_769                 Nay!
Christof_21_1_770               Christof_21_1_770               Aye! 'Tis so.
Luther_21_1_771                 Luther_21_1_771                 Aye. Tis so. Wilt thou do this for me all the same? It is more than I may ask of thee, yet I ask it still. Wilt thou take my sins upon thee?
Christof_21_1_772               Christof_21_1_772               Very well then. We shall bind thee.
Christof_21_1_773               Christof_21_1_773               Nay. I shall not. Not even to regain Anezka.
Luther_21_1_774                 Luther_21_1_774                 Bind me with Orsi's chain, that I cannot escape the sun in my frenzy.
Luther_21_1_775                 Luther_21_1_775                 Coward! If thou art too craven to do the act for which thou hast defiled my sanctum, I shall do the deed myself, and remove the stain of us all!
Serena_21_1_742                 Serena_21_1_742                 The Lasombra obsess over portraiture, since they can no longer cast reflections into mirrors.
Wilhem_21_1_743                 Wilhem_21_1_743                 'Tis a mysterious quirk of Caine's blood.
Christof_21_1_740               Christof_21_1_740               Shadows darker than night linger here.
Christof_21_1_741               Christof_21_1_741               Even within the depths of such an evil place, there is a heart of beauty.
Christof_22_3_800               Christof_22_3_800               What do these strange omens portend?
Erik_22_1_794                   Erik_22_1_794                   Free! How sweet is freedom!
Wilhem_22_1_795                 Wilhem_22_1_795                 I have a score to settle with those Teutonic Knights. They reflect badly on my homeland, and I must smite them before the locals think we are all ignoble knaves!
Erik_22_1_796                   Erik_22_1_796                   Freedom is sweet, and their blood shall be the sweeter!
Christof_22_1_781               Christof_22_1_781               At least tell me if the Tremere have harmed Anezka!
Orsi_22_1_782                   Orsi_22_1_782                   That's thy only concern as thou art being taken as a slave? The health of some other slave? Thou must develop thy self-interest if thou wish to survive the ordeal.
Christof_22_1_783               Christof_22_1_783               Tell me if Anezka has been harmed!
Orsi_22_1_784                   Orsi_22_1_784                   Oh, who can keep track of such things? When the silver poureth in like water, I have not the time to track every slave.
Christof_22_1_785               Christof_22_1_785               If Anezka has been harmed, I will destroy thee in the most painful manner possible, even if it takes a thousand years!
Orsi_22_1_786                   Orsi_22_1_786                   Thou art impertinent for a slave. We shall see how a few weeks of starvation calms thy hot blood.
Christof_22_1_787               Christof_22_1_787               Thou hast heard my oath, thou depraved peddler of living flesh!
Orsi_22_1_788                   Orsi_22_1_788                   Well. Humph. I have spent too much time with thee. Humph.
Erik_22_1_789                   Erik_22_1_789                   Arrr! I cannot shatter this cage!
Wilhem_22_1_790                 Wilhem_22_1_790                 It seems impenetrable!
Erik_22_1_791                   Erik_22_1_791                   Noooo! I will not go back to a Tremere dungeon!
Serena_22_1_792                 Serena_22_1_792                 Then lend me a bit of thy blood. I have a plan, but need all my strength to make it happen.
Christof_22_1_793               Christof_22_1_793               Take all thou needs.
Teutonic_22_2_797               Teutonic_22_2_797               The slaves are free!
Teutonic_22_2_798               Teutonic_22_2_798               Capture them! Do not let them escape!
Serena_22_2_799                 Serena_22_2_799                 Why escape when we can stay and feast on thy soft, warm blood?
Wilhem_22_4_808                 Wilhem_22_4_808                 There are Tremere here, allied with the Teutonic Knights toward some fell purpose.
Erik_22_4_809                   Erik_22_4_809                   Maps. They show strikes against the Tzimisce throughout the forest and nearby lands.
Serena_22_4_810                 Serena_22_4_810                 This fortress appears to be the seat of the Ventrue and Tremere alliance against the fiends.
Wilhem_22_4_811                 Wilhem_22_4_811                 We must tell this to Ecaterina.
Christof_22_5_817               Christof_22_5_817               What dost thou know of the Haus de Hexe?
Orvus_22_5_818                  Orvus_22_5_818                  Only that the magi within were once part of our Order, but have of late been up to doings unknown, allowing none entry to their fortress. The Order would be grateful for anything that thou may learn of them. Or do to them.
Christof_22_5_819               Christof_22_5_819               We cannot enter the fortress either.
Orvus_22_5_820                  Orvus_22_5_820                  Thou needs must have the Amulet of Etrius.
Christof_22_5_821               Christof_22_5_821               Amulet? We found this amulet with the Tremere.
Orvus_22_5_822                  Orvus_22_5_822                  This is the very thing. Yet it needs must be filled with magic to work. I will enchant it if thou promise to return with the Journal of Etrius.
Christof_22_5_823               Christof_22_5_823               Why seek you this journal, Orvus?
Orvus_22_5_824                  Orvus_22_5_824                  We seek to cleanse our Hermetic Order of the taint of the Tremere. And we must learn more about the frightening loss of magic in the world that began at the turn of the millennium. Magic fades from the world, and we know not how to stop the inexorable ebb of the magical tides. The Tremere have learned some of these secrets, but will not share them.
Christof_22_5_825               Christof_22_5_825               If we find such a journal we shall give it thee.
Orvus_22_5_826                  Orvus_22_5_826                  Then I shall enchant thy Amulet of Etrius.
Orvus_22_5_827                  Orvus_22_5_827                  Go quickly. The Tremere are invading Tzimisce territory this night to launch open warfare, leaving their Chantry largely unguarded. I wish thee luck.
Christof_22_5_828               Christof_22_5_828               I thank thee, Orvus. Now let us split asunder Das Haus Die Hexe.
Christof_23_2_842               Christof_23_2_842               Where are the slaves? Where is Anezka?
DATrem2_23_2_843                DATrem2_23_2_843                Hold! How didst thou enter?
DATrem2_23_2_844                DATrem2_23_2_844                Intruders in our sanctum! Bring them down!
Etrius_23_6_861                 Etrius_23_6_861                 Well. Well, well. When the cat is away, the rats come out to play. The luck of the gods is with thee, for on any other night the full force of Tremere would have dissolved thee into slop. Flee this place now, or thy deaths shall be as vile as thine offenses.
Christof_23_6_862               Christof_23_6_862               Where are the slaves? Where is Anezka?
Etrius_23_6_863                 Etrius_23_6_863                 Fools! I have no time for thee! I must return to the war against the vile Tzimisce. Dost thou not understand my charity in allowing thee to flee with thy miserable hides intact? Go now!
Christof_23_6_864               Christof_23_6_864               Give us the slaves.
Erik_23_6_865                   Erik_23_6_865                   Or look to protect thine own hide.
Etrius_23_6_866                 Etrius_23_6_866                 What?! Heh. Thy temerity is exceeded only by thy folly. Etrius is beyond thy harm.
Erik_23_6_867                   Erik_23_6_867                   He is not. But prithee wait. For Erik can ensure that Etrius is forever beyond all harm.
Etrius_23_6_868                 Etrius_23_6_868                 I shall remember thy insolence, ancient Gangrel.
Christof_23_6_869               Christof_23_6_869               There is no need for further bloodshed. I wish thy Brujah slaves and the mortal woman Anezka, from the October caravan, and we shall leave this house in peace.
Etrius_23_6_870                 Etrius_23_6_870                 And if I give them not?
Erik_23_6_871                   Erik_23_6_871                   Then I shall pop thy baldy pate between my teeth like an overripe melon!
Etrius_23_6_872                 Etrius_23_6_872                 I warned thee, Gangrel! Thou hast nearly completed the cycle of transformation in Ardan's Chantry! Now I finish his work. Behold the power of the Tremere!
Erik_23_6_873                   Erik_23_6_873                   Mmfmfmfgh!
Christof_23_6_874               Christof_23_6_874               Rest in peace, my friend. Thy wrongful death will be avenged!
Etrius_23_6_875                 Etrius_23_6_875                 Thou hast killed the Gangrel? Is this how Christof rewards his faithful allies? Now I will sheath my fangs in thy disloyal neck, whelp!
Christof_23_6_876               Christof_23_6_876               Is he dead?
Etrius_23_6_877                 Etrius_23_6_877                 Curse thee, boy! I have suffered the loss of precious magic in my world! I have suffered the willing loss of my soul to retain some spark of enchantment in a world turned to dross! I have suffered the maddening serenity of the dying Salout! But I will not suffer further indignity at the hands of a fledgling Brujah and his rag-tag brigade! Hear me, Promethian! Thy precious Anezka is not here! The October caravan from that idiot Orsi never reached the Haus De Hexe! The hated Tzimisce laid a trap near Prague. They took the caravan and all therein. The Tzimisce are the real foe in this world! Even as thou waste my time, the fiends plot to burn the world down around us all! Now go! And disturb us no further!
Christof_23_6_878               Christof_23_6_878               I have wanted no part of any of the schemes of the undead, yet I have risked myself in all of them! And has it brought me one step closer to Anezka? Has it gained me a jot more humanity?
Wilhem_23_6_879                 Wilhem_23_6_879                 I cannot answer thee.
Serena_23_6_880                 Serena_23_6_880                 Oh, Christof. My heart aches for thee.
Wilhem_23_2_845                 Wilhem_23_2_845                 These carvings are strangely similar to the designs in the entry hall.
Serena_23_2_846                 Serena_23_2_846                 Methinks they are tumblers in a magical lock.
Erik_23_3_847                   Erik_23_3_847                   Arrgh! I hate these wretched gargoyles!
Serena_23_1_840                 Serena_23_1_840                 The Amulet of Etrius works!
Erik_23_1_841                   Erik_23_1_841                   That is well. I did not wish to have to eat the runty little Orvus.
Serena_23_1_829                 Serena_23_1_829                 Such a cold and forbidding place.
Erik_23_1_830                   Erik_23_1_830                   I like not the look of the spikes on the portcullis.
Wilhem_23_1_831                 Wilhem_23_1_831                 We must proceed with care.
Christof_23_1_832               Christof_23_1_832               Pray do not falter with our destination so close at hand.
Serena_23_1_833                 Serena_23_1_833                 The bridge is studded with iron.
Wilhem_23_1_834                 Wilhem_23_1_834                 Iron? They must fear the creatures of the fae.
Erik_23_1_835                   Erik_23_1_835                   And silver. They fear werewolves as well. Though I regret that they have found the secret weakness of the Lupines.
Christof_23_1_836               Christof_23_1_836               'Tis their sorrow that they have no element for keeping out Cainites. Come.
Erik_23_1_837                   Erik_23_1_837                   A stench of rotting meat from below.
Wilhem_23_1_838                 Wilhem_23_1_838                 No doubt we are not the first to try to assail the Tremere.
Serena_23_1_839                 Serena_23_1_839                 Merely the first to succeed.
Wilhem_23_4_853                 Wilhem_23_4_853                 More hideous experiments!
Erik_23_4_854                   Erik_23_4_854                   I loathe all mages!
Christof_23_4_855               Christof_23_4_855               Where are the slaves? Where is Anezka?
DATrem2_23_4_856                DATrem2_23_4_856                Interlopers!
DATrem2_23_4_857                DATrem2_23_4_857                Mongrels have strayed in our Haus Die Hexe! Bring them to heel!
Christof_23_5_858               Christof_23_5_858               Where are the slaves? Where is Anezka? Tell me, and thou shalt not be harmed!
DATrem2_23_5_859                DATrem2_23_5_859                I know not why thou intrudes upon my workshop, or by what darkling sorcery thou hast overcome our wards. But pray do not tell me. I shall be far more delighted to read the answers in the twisted strands and moist fragments of thy entrails.
Orvus_23_7_882                  Orvus_23_7_882                  We give thanks to thee. To show our gratitude, we give thee an enchantment that will help thee deflect flame. The journal of Etrius should prove helpful in cleansing our Order of this vile infiltration.
Christof_23_7_883               Christof_23_7_883               And thy gift should prove helpful in the fiery future we all face.
Christof_23_3_848               Christof_23_3_848               Where are the slaves? Where is Anezka? Tell me, and thou shalt not be harmed!
Virst_23_3_849                  Virst_23_3_849                  Meddling coster-mongers! Thou cannot comprehend the forces thou hast interrupted!
Christof_23_3_850               Christof_23_3_850               And for that small mercy we give thanks.
Virst_23_3_851                  Virst_23_3_851                  I shall destroy thee, and seek out thy progeny for torture and thy allies for enslavement!
Erik_23_3_852                   Erik_23_3_852                   One thing at a time, Virstania. Thou has yet to deal with us.
Christof_25_1_888               Christof_25_1_888               What madness is this?
Ecat_25_1_889                   Ecat_25_1_889                   The battle has begun. The city is under siege by vampires and mortals alike. Prince Rudolf is slain. The Tzimisce within Vysehrad castle have been revealed to the townspeople, who even now mount a witch-burning campaign against the them and all Kindred. The castle will not stand! We have won!
Christof_25_1_891               Christof_25_1_891               Anezka may be prisoner of the Tzimisce! We must fly to Vysehrad castle!
Ecat_25_1_892                   Ecat_25_1_892                   Thou hast grown strong, Childe. Thou hast learned to harness the gifts I have bequeathed thee. But this evil is far greater than any thou hast known. Vysehrad is a tomb! I forbid a venture there, and all who enter will surely die!
Christof_25_1_893               Christof_25_1_893               I am already dead, thanks to thee! Or didst thou forget? Now I go!
Serena_25_1_894                 Serena_25_1_894                 Wait, Christof! I join thee.
Wilhem_25_1_895                 Wilhem_25_1_895                 Sorry, Ecaterina. I cannot abandon him now.
Ecat_25_1_896                   Ecat_25_1_896                   Poor fool, Wilhem. I thought thou wouldst teach Christof. Now I see thou art the pupil, and Christof the teacher. Mayhap his futile quest shall lead thee to thy demise.
Christof_26_4_914               Christof_26_4_914               Anezka! I sought thee for love!
Anezka_26_4_913                 Anezka_26_4_913                 So predictable. So pathetically predictable. Like all oafish mortal men, thou come a-trotting when a woman beckons.
Anezka_26_4_915                 Anezka_26_4_915                 Oh, how thy sinful words offend mine ears. Did not thy carnal lusts die with thy mortal flesh?
Christof_26_4_916               Christof_26_4_916               Love! Love that is pure. Love can release thee!
Anezka_26_4_917                 Anezka_26_4_917                 Fool! Only the bards and the diseased of mind pay heed to such rot.
Christof_26_4_918               Christof_26_4_918               O fair Anezka! What have they done to thee?
Anezka_26_4_919                 Anezka_26_4_919                 All manner of delightful things! I am thoroughly defiled now, and it is all because of thee!
Christof_26_4_920               Christof_26_4_920               Forgive me, Anezka. I never meant harm to come to thee.
Anezka_26_4_921                 Anezka_26_4_921                 But thou harmed me all the same! I will enjoy the taste of thy Brujah blood. It is so clean, compared to the sweet corruption of Tzimisce blood. Bid the Devil greetings from me, for I send thee to hell!
Vukodlak_26_4_922               Vukodlak_26_4_922               Anezka is mine now whelp, another of my servants that await me in my slumber. Even now she grows strong as my blood courses through her veins. As I rise to meet the night sky of the new millennium, the very Antediluvians will shudder in fear.
Anezka_26_4_923                 Anezka_26_4_923                 Fool! Release me!
Christof_26_4_924               Christof_26_4_924               I shall protect thee from these monsters.
Anezka_26_4_925                 Anezka_26_4_925                 I have a ceremony of resurrection to perform! Begone!
Christof_26_4_926               Christof_26_4_926               Nay.
Anezka_26_4_927                 Anezka_26_4_927                 The walls fall about us! Release me!
Christof_26_4_928               Christof_26_4_928               Never.
Christof_26_4_929               Christof_26_4_929               Anezka!
Christof_26_2_897               Christof_26_2_897               Where is she? Where is Anezka!
Rev1_26_2_898                   Rev1_26_2_898                   'Tis Christof! Kill him!
Rev1_26_2_899                   Rev1_26_2_899                   Christof! The murderer of Ahzra!
Rev2_26_2_900                   Rev2_26_2_900                   Christof! The butcher of countless Premysls!
Rev3_26_2_901                   Rev3_26_2_901                   Christof! Ravager of the impenetrable Tremere fortress!
Rev4_26_2_902                   Rev4_26_2_902                   Perhaps we should flee!
Rev1_26_2_903                   Rev1_26_2_903                   Fools! He's only a fledgling! Kill him!
Christof_26_2_904               Christof_26_2_904               Come, fools! Thy Final Death awaits.
PragueReb_25_2_2525             PragueReb_25_2_2525             Good people of Prague! For too many years have we trembled in the shadow of this hell-hated mountain! Let us wage bloody war upon these fiends! I pray that our righteous fires burn this wicked castle to the roots and cleanse the land of all evil-doers!
Christof_27_2_944               Christof_27_2_944               Where am I? What sorcerer's abode is this?
Christof_27_2_945               Christof_27_2_945               Anezka...
Leo_27_4_962                    Leo_27_4_962                    Hello, filthy little Kindred. I am Father Leo Allatius, and I have killed bloodsuckers like you for two hundred years!
Christof_27_4_963               Christof_27_4_963               I have no wish to fight thee.
Leo_27_4_964                    Leo_27_4_964                    Then give up your blood without a fight!  It will make a tasty addition to my collection. Early generation Kindred. Vintage Twelfth Century. Eleven forty? A good decade for vitae!
Christof_27_4_965               Christof_27_4_965               I wish only to leave this place. But I will kill thee if I must.
Leo_27_4_966                    Leo_27_4_966                    Your time is dead, boy! You can never fit in to this world! You have no one! You are nothing! Let us deliver you from this alien land of eternal loneliness and pain!
Christof_27_4_967               Christof_27_4_967               I did not endure for eight hundred years to die at thy behest.
Christof_27_1_933               Christof_27_1_933               Where is she?
Society1_27_1_934               Society1_27_1_934               Who?
Christof_27_1_935               Christof_27_1_935               Trifle not with me, servant of the Tzimisce, for the hunger is so great in me I would gladly squeeze all thy blood from thee and still not be sated! Where is Anezka?
Society1_27_1_936               Society1_27_1_936               I don't know any Anezka!
Christof_27_1_937               Christof_27_1_937               Where is thy master? For if such a one as I survived, surely the ancient Vukodlak endures still.
Society1_27_1_938               Society1_27_1_938               I don't know anybody named Vukodlak!
Christof_27_1_939               Christof_27_1_939               Thou speakest the language of England, but in a manner most passing strange. Who is thy master, mortal?
Society1_27_1_940               Society1_27_1_940               I'm with the Society of Leopold.
Christof_27_1_941               Christof_27_1_941               I know them not.
Society1_27_1_942               Society1_27_1_942               We slay vampires!
Christof_27_1_943               Christof_27_1_943               My name is Christof Romuald. I was a man of God, and a soldier in Heaven's cause. I am now outcast of heaven, and not even a man. I am Kindred. I am a Vampire.
Christof_27_2_2533              Christof_27_2_2533              A metal sling that hurls deadly stones. 'Tis simple to use, yet murderous beyond measure.  I see that man has not rested in his quest to create ever more powerful weapons.
Leo_27_4_968                    Leo_27_4_968                    Nay! My vitae! My precious vitae! Stop! Please! I'll die without it!
Christof_27_4_969               Christof_27_4_969               Wretched fool. Thou seekest not the safety of mortals. Thou seeks only thine own exaltation. How little men have changed in a thousand years.
Society2_27_3_949               Society2_27_3_949               Who is that?
Society3_27_3_950               Society3_27_3_950               A vampire! Kill him!
Society2_27_3_951               Society2_27_3_951               Back off, bloodsucker! I'm sending you to hell!
Christof_27_3_961               Christof_27_3_961               Look how all the world hath aged. And I have aged too. I feel old and drained and weathered as all these relics.
MDBart1_28_1_1916               MDBart1_28_1_1916               We have a wide selection of vitae for your dining pleasure. We have blue collar brews, white collar cocktails, and pink collar daiquiris. We've got young blood, old blood, tainted blood and blue blood. We've got innocence, we've got experience, uptown, downtown, Park Avenue matrons and Bowery winos. Our special of the day is a succulent free range virgin fresh off the bus from Iowa, free of additives and preservatives. You'll find it a tart blend, with a crisp and refreshing afterbite.
Christof_28_1_970               Christof_28_1_970               Now is all my reason thrown down. Surely, my sleep hath made me mad. For if I am yet sane, then the world is become a lunatic asylum. Towers of glass loom over the tallest cathedral spires. Juggernauts of steel hurtle through the streets of London. The cobbled Roman roads, which once I walked as a young crusader, are now fused into a single ribbon of black stone. And those roads are clogged with night-walking Londoners, heedless of the danger from the vampires among them. Are they so emboldened by the phantom torches which pierce the night and stab my eyes? Surely my world has died, and all I love lies buried with it.
Pink_28_3_980                   Pink_28_3_980                   Bottoms up. Ah! Blood's a bit di-looted 'ere, ay? Wot, you fresh out the grave? Newly Embraced? You look it, with that deer-in-the-'eadlights look pasted on your gob.
Christof_28_3_981               Christof_28_3_981               Do not presume to mock me, whelp! I am far older than thou knowest, and have no patience for the likes of thee.
Pink_28_3_982                   Pink_28_3_982                   Well, well, well. Hey! Barkeep! Get this antique bloodsucker a swig a' vitae, courtesy of Pink of Clan Brujah! And don't water it down, ya mortal worm!
Pink_28_3_983                   Pink_28_3_983                   This will put some color back in yer cheeks! Hair o' the bat that bit ya!
Christof_28_3_984               Christof_28_3_984               Thou art Brujah? Art thou a Promethian?
Pink_28_3_985                   Pink_28_3_985                   Haw! You MUST be a fossil. The Promethians are ancient history. Those nutters are long dead, along with their utopian ideals. What a load a batshit that was! What's yer name, ya crusty ol' relic?
Christof_28_3_986               Christof_28_3_986               Forgive me. I am Christof Romuald.
Pink_28_3_987                   Pink_28_3_987                   Ooo, Christof Romuald.
Christof_28_3_988               Christof_28_3_988               Christof Romuald, once of the Order of the Swordbrethren, once a Promethian Brujah, and now... now I know not what. Weary. Alone. And damned!
Pink_28_3_989                   Pink_28_3_989                   Damned I can't 'elp! But no one is alone wiv' old Pink around! Especially not a fellow Brujah!  'Ere's to Christof, the last a' the Promethians! Welcome to the New World, Squire! 'Ope you like what we done wiv' the place!
Pink_28_3_990                   Pink_28_3_990                   So where will you be creatin' your Promethian paradise on earth, Squire?
Christof_28_3_991               Christof_28_3_991               All I wanted was to be with my Anezka.
Pink_28_3_992                   Pink_28_3_992                   Bit a' crumpet? I've heard of worse paradises, an' no mistake!
Christof_28_3_993               Christof_28_3_993               But fair Anezka was taken as Ghoul by that Tzimisce monster, Vukodlak! After such horrors as I have endured, after losing so much, I awake to find I have finally lost ALL. For I have lost her.
Pink_28_3_994                   Pink_28_3_994                   Ere! Not so fast, Squire! There's two ways your bird might be around. Ghouls can live as long as us licks. 'Course, she'd need a constant supply of Tzimisce blood or she'll fall apart faster than Thatcher's reforms. And if one a' them fiends embraced her, she's be around today as one of us! Well... as a Tzimisce.
Christof_28_3_995               Christof_28_3_995               Thou dost compound my misery! I dare not hope such a thing. 'Twould be a curse if fair Anezka lived in such a state for a thousand years.
Pink_28_3_996                   Pink_28_3_996                   Take it from 'ol Pink. Anything's better than the quiet of the grave. There's hope even for us licks. We can climb the path to the summit... uh.. or some such.
Christof_28_3_997               Christof_28_3_997               Thou art on the Road of Humanitas?
Pink_28_3_998                   Pink_28_3_998                   Mmm...Something like that.
Christof_28_3_999               Christof_28_3_999               Thou speakest true. Should Anezka have been preserved for lo these many centuries, I shall seek after her. Whether she is ghoul to that monster Vukodlak, or one of his vampires, I shall find her. Find her and destroy him! He will pay in angry blood! And if I find only her grave, I shall... I shall be exceeding glad for her soul.
Pink_28_3_1000                  Pink_28_3_1000                  Rare thing, such passion in licks. Bloodless pack a' cowards these days. Tell you wot. I'll help you find this bird, Anezka. I hates the Tzimisces, too. I could enjoy sinkin' me fangs into a fiend or two.
Christof_28_3_1001              Christof_28_3_1001              I need no one.
Christof_28_3_1002              Christof_28_3_1002              Milord Pink, thou art honorable. I accept thy kindly offer.
Pink_28_3_1003                  Pink_28_3_1003                  Try and stop me!
Pink_28_3_1004                  Pink_28_3_1004                  You'll need me to tell you wot's wot. The Camarilla have a million little rules. Wipe ya' self wiv' the wrong hand, and these licks will call down the Justicars on you!
Christof_28_3_1005              Christof_28_3_1005              What?
Pink_28_3_1006                  Pink_28_3_1006                  Noffing. Just a joke.
Christof_28_3_1007              Christof_28_3_1007              Thou art unlike the vampires of my world, for most only assisted me for their personal gain.
Pink_28_3_1008                  Pink_28_3_1008                  Well, what's left of us Brujah got to stick together. Even if yer a moldy ol' fossil. So. Where did ya last see this bird a' yours?
Christof_28_3_1009              Christof_28_3_1009              I last beheld Anezka before the collapse of the Tzimisce stronghold in Prague. I have since learned that the Tzimisce have traveled from thence to London, and by sea to a land west of London, called New York. Perhaps this New York lies within Ireland.
Pink_28_3_1010                  Pink_28_3_1010                  Haw! No. Ever since the famine, Ireland lies within New York! Haw haw!
Christof_28_3_1011              Christof_28_3_1011              There are isles west of Ireland?
Pink_28_3_1012                  Pink_28_3_1012                  Something like that. Little place called America. The United States thereof.
Christof_28_3_1013              Christof_28_3_1013              United States. An auspicious name. For I wish my own state reunited.
Pink_28_3_1014                  Pink_28_3_1014                  Aw. Yer breakin' my heart. .
Christof_28_3_1015              Christof_28_3_1015              Perhaps in New York shall we find a criminal named Giovanni.
Pink_28_3_1016                  Pink_28_3_1016                  Giovanni? They ain't one guy. They're a whole Clan! A whole clan a' criminals! They snacked on ol' Cappadocious, and sucked down all his juice. The entire Cappadocian Clan is gone, and the Giovanni have their power.
Christof_28_3_1017              Christof_28_3_1017              Hmmm. I am not surprised. The Cappadocian Clan seemed oddly gullible and ripe for domination by schemers even in my day. What became of the Brujah?
Pink_28_3_1018                  Pink_28_3_1018                  Wot hasn't! The Brujah are all kissed and made up with the Ventrue now, in one big happy family called the Camarilla. The Toreador, the Gangrel, the Nosferatu, the loony Malkavians... even the Tremere are bosom buddies. Outta fear of Gehenna, mostly. Our real enemy is the Sabbat- made up of the Tzimisce, the Lasombra, and a pack of the most vicious licks in the world! I don't care for the snobs of the Camarilla any more than the next lick, but I don't wanna dig my way out of a bloody grave. That's what the Sabbat do to you, beat you to the brink of death, then bury you. When you start starving, you claw your way to the surface, the madness killing any bit of humanity in you. So I work with the Camarilla against the Sabbat.
Christof_28_3_1019              Christof_28_3_1019              My past is dead, and I am no longer a pawn servicing the whims of the Elders in their Jyhad.
Pink_28_3_1020                  Pink_28_3_1020                  It ain't good to be alone out there. It helps to have a gang at your back! Especially if you wanna find this Anezka. I can't help you find the Giovanni, but I can help you find out about any bootleg shipping. The filthy Setites run all the bootleg shipping in London. I know a Setite knocking shop on the East End. Now let's put the boot into some snakes! But watch yourself. The Setites are a real bad seed.
Christof_28_3_1021              Christof_28_3_1021              Knocking shop?
Pink_28_3_1022                  Pink_28_3_1022                  I know you had 'em in your day, Chris. Even a geezer like you can't be older than the world's oldest profession. Now come on. We're gonna need supplies. You can sell some a' that old junk and get some real weapons. Me mate Otto will fix you up a treat! He's got an arsenal in that old van down under the bridge. Just remember ta knock carefully. He's a mite jumpy from an old war wound... to his head! Har har!
Christof_28_3_1023              Christof_28_3_1023              We require an armorer and an alchemist.
Pink_28_3_1024                  Pink_28_3_1024                  Ah...something like that.
Christof_28_1_2534              Christof_28_1_2534              My garments have moldered away with age, as my body would have, were I not one of the damned. I cannot wander the streets clad thus.  I have need of suitable garments.
Mugger_28_1_2535                Mugger_28_1_2535                Oi! You need a lot more than some new clothes, ya freak. You need to hand over yer wallet!
